# just-terminal DEV — in-instance loopback hop for the HOST Caddy (dev instance).
#
# Topology:
#   Browser
#     -> host Caddy            ({instance}.js.actor)
#     -> THIS Caddy            (10.66.204.209:8091, instance IP — reachable by host)
#     -> just-terminal dev           (127.0.0.1:8312, loopback)
#
# Production runs on :9090 via systemd (binary: ~/.local/bin/just-terminal).
# Dev runs on :9091 via `make dev` / air (binary: ./bin/just-terminal).
# The two never conflict: different binary, different port, different host URL.
#
# Why this hop exists: just-terminal's SPA carries no auth token; it relies on the
# server's localhost auth-bypass (internal/server/auth.go IsLocalhost). The host
# Caddy connects from a non-loopback IP, which would force a 30s token the SPA
# can't supply. By terminating here and dialing just-terminal over 127.0.0.1, just-terminal
# always sees a loopback peer, so remote users get in token-free. WebSocket
# upgrades (tmux control mode) pass through reverse_proxy automatically.
#
# Run with:  caddy run --config ./Caddyfile   (started for you by `make dev`)

:8091 {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:9091

	log {
		output file ./tmp/caddy.log
		format console
	}
}
